<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>DevOps Learning Guide</title>

<style>
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background: #0f172a;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    line-height: 1.7;
}

header {
    background: #1e293b;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 50px 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #38bdf8;
}

header h1 {
    font-size: 38px;
    color: #38bdf8;
}

header p {
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: #cbd5e1;
}

nav {
    background: #111827;
    padding: 15px;
    text-align: center;
}

nav a {
    color: #38bdf8;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin: 10px;
}

.container {
    width: 90%;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 30px 0;
}

section {
    margin-bottom: 35px;
}

h2 {
    color: #38bdf8;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #334155;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
}

.card {
    background: #1e293b;
    padding: 20px;
    margin: 15px 0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid #334155;
}

.card h3 {
    color: #f8fafc;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}

ul {
    padding-left: 25px;
}

li {
    margin-bottom: 7px;
}

.highlight {
    color: #38bdf8;
}

footer {
    text-align: center;
    background: #111827;
    padding: 25px;
    color: #94a3b8;
}

button {
    background: #0284c7;
    color: white;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
}

button:hover {
    background: #0369a1;
}

</style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
    <h1>DevOps Learning Guide</h1>
    <p>Learn, Build, Automate and Deploy</p>
    <p>My journey towards becoming a DevOps Engineer</p>
</header>

<nav>
    <a href="#intro">Introduction</a>
    <a href="#tools">Tools</a>
    <a href="#cloud">Cloud</a>
    <a href="#pipeline">CI/CD</a>
    <a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a>
</nav>

<div class="container">

<section id="intro">
    <h2>Introduction to DevOps</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>What is DevOps?</h3>
        <p>
            DevOps is a combination of development and operations practices
            that helps teams build, test, release and maintain software
            faster and more reliably.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Why DevOps?</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Faster software delivery</li>
            <li>Better teamwork</li>
            <li>Automation of repetitive tasks</li>
            <li>Reliable software deployment</li>
            <li>Continuous improvement</li>
            <li>Reduced manual errors</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="tools">
    <h2>DevOps Tools</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Git</h3>
        <p>Git is a version control system used to track changes in source code.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>GitHub</h3>
        <p>GitHub provides a platform for storing code, collaboration and project management.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Docker</h3>
        <p>Docker allows applications to run inside containers with their dependencies.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Jenkins</h3>
        <p>Jenkins is an automation server used for building and testing software.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Kubernetes</h3>
        <p>Kubernetes helps manage, scale and orchestrate containerized applications.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Ansible</h3>
        <p>Ansible automates server configuration and infrastructure management.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Terraform</h3>
        <p>Terraform is an Infrastructure as Code tool used to provision cloud resources.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="cloud">
    <h2>Cloud Computing</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>What is Cloud Computing?</h3>
        <p>
            Cloud computing provides computing resources such as servers,
            databases, storage and networking over the internet.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Cloud Service Models</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>IaaS - Infrastructure as a Service</li>
            <li>PaaS - Platform as a Service</li>
            <li>SaaS - Software as a Service</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Cloud Providers</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</li>
            <li>Microsoft Azure</li>
            <li>Google Cloud Platform (GCP)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="pipeline">
    <h2>CI/CD Pipeline</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Continuous Integration</h3>
        <p>
            Developers regularly merge code changes into a shared repository.
            Automated builds and tests help detect problems early.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Continuous Delivery</h3>
        <p>
            The software is kept ready for release through automated
            build, testing and deployment preparation.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Continuous Deployment</h3>
        <p>
            Changes that pass the required automated checks can be
            deployed automatically to the production environment.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Pipeline Stages</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Source Code</li>
            <li>Build</li>
            <li>Test</li>
            <li>Quality Check</li>
            <li>Package</li>
            <li>Deploy</li>
            <li>Monitor</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Linux & Networking</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Linux Basics</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>File system structure</li>
            <li>File permissions</li>
            <li>Users and groups</li>
            <li>Process management</li>
            <li>Shell scripting</li>
            <li>Package management</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Networking Concepts</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>IP Address</li>
            <li>MAC Address</li>
            <li>DNS</li>
            <li>HTTP and HTTPS</li>
            <li>TCP and UDP</li>
            <li>Ports</li>
            <li>Firewall</li>
            <li>Load Balancer</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Monitoring & Logging</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Monitoring</h3>
        <p>
            Monitoring helps track application health, server performance,
            resource usage and availability.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>CPU usage</li>
            <li>Memory usage</li>
            <li>Disk utilization</li>
            <li>Network traffic</li>
            <li>Application response time</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Popular Monitoring Tools</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Prometheus</li>
            <li>Grafana</li>
            <li>ELK Stack</li>
            <li>Datadog</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="roadmap">
    <h2>DevOps Learning Roadmap</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 1 - Fundamentals</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Computer Networks</li>
            <li>Linux</li>
            <li>Git and GitHub</li>
            <li>Basic scripting</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 2 - Development</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>HTML and CSS</li>
            <li>JavaScript</li>
            <li>Backend fundamentals</li>
            <li>APIs</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 3 - Automation</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>CI/CD</li>
            <li>Jenkins</li>
            <li>Automated testing</li>
            <li>Build tools</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 4 - Containers</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Docker</li>
            <li>Docker Images</li>
            <li>Docker Containers</li>
            <li>Docker Compose</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 5 - Cloud</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>AWS Fundamentals</li>
            <li>EC2</li>
            <li>S3</li>
            <li>IAM</li>
            <li>VPC</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Phase 6 - Orchestration</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Kubernetes</li>
            <li>Pods</li>
            <li>Deployments</li>
            <li>Services</li>
            <li>Scaling</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>My DevOps Goals</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <ul>
            <li>Improve my Linux knowledge</li>
            <li>Understand Git deeply</li>
            <li>Build CI/CD pipelines</li>
            <li>Learn Docker</li>
            <li>Explore AWS</li>
            <li>Deploy real-world applications</li>
            <li>Practice automation</li>
            <li>Build hands-on projects</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Learning Quote</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="highlight">
            Learn continuously. Build consistently.
            Automate intelligently.
        </h3>

        <p>
            Every small project is a step towards mastering technology.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

</div>

<footer>
    <p>DevOps Learning Guide | Learning by Building</p>
    <p>Version 1.0 | 2026</p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
